    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is a modular spiral conveyor?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "A modular spiral conveyor is assembled from standard, factory-built components: tier sections, support columns, a drive unit, and infeed and discharge ends. Height changes by adding or removing tiers, and the unit can be moved or reconfigured later. The tradeoff is that sizes are limited to the supplier's standard widths, diameters, and pitches. The term is also used for spirals that run on modular plastic belt, so confirm which meaning a supplier intends." }
    },
    {
